OL,3,GNEWSAGrade II-listed windmill returned
OL,4,Ato white after colourful makeover
OL,5,
OL,6,FWales' only working windmill has been
OL,7,Freturned to its original white colour
OL,8,Fafter its owner broke council rules by
OL,9,Fpainting it red, white and green
OL,10,Fwithout permission.
OL,12,FMelin Llynon, on Anglesey, was given a
OL,13,Fmakeover in Welsh colours to mark the
OL,14,Fisland hosting youth movement Urdd
OL,15,FGobaith Cymru's Eisteddfod.
OL,17,FOwner Richard Holt said he had intended
OL,18,Fto return the 250-year-old Grade
OL,19,FII-listed mill to its original white
OL,20,Fafter the week-long festival of music,
OL,21,Fdance and literature, but positive
OL,22,Freaction had stopped him.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
